# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 06-error-cases.http — Negative path / error response api-coverage
#
# Run order: after 01-auth.http at minimum; some cases require groupId/promptId.
#
# These requests are EXPECTED to fail. Verify the HTTP status code and that
# the response body is RFC 9457 Problem Details JSON
# (fields: type, title, status, detail, instance).
#
# Grouped by error category:
#   401 — Unauthenticated access
#   400 — Bean validation failures
#   400 — Malformed / type-mismatch input
#   404 — Resource not found
#   409 — Conflict
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 401 Unauthenticated ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [401-1] Missing Authorization header on protected endpoint
# Expected: 401 Unauthorized

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/groups

> {%
    client.test("Missing Authorization on groups returns 401", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, `Expected 401 Unauthorized but received ${response.status}`);
    });
%}

###

